WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.260
- [Narrator] Politics are a powerful

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:07.420
and dynamic human creation,
a truth most evident

00:00:08.491 --> 00:00:10.983
in revolutions around the world.

00:00:13.189 --> 00:00:15.688
A revolution, in a political sense,

00:00:15.688 --> 00:00:17.668
is a sudden and seismic shift

00:00:17.668 --> 00:00:20.899
from one form of government to another.

00:00:20.899 --> 00:00:23.658
While revolutions come in many forms,

00:00:23.658 --> 00:00:28.120
they often share four
characteristcis in varying degrees.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.360
Dissident elites, mass frustration,

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.834
shared motivation, and state crises.

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:36.438
All together, these factors have ignited

00:00:36.438 --> 00:00:39.943
some of the most radical
changes throughout history.

00:00:40.824 --> 00:00:45.429
Revolutions are often
facilitated by a dissident elite.

00:00:45.429 --> 00:00:48.710
This particular group
is comprised of people

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.069
with wealth, power, or an education

00:00:51.069 --> 00:00:54.403
who are willing to challenge
the existing adminisitration.

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:58.189
Elites played a critical role
in the American Revolution,

00:00:58.189 --> 00:01:01.433
one of the earliest
revolutions in modern history.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:05.008
American colonists, under
the rule of Great Britain,

00:01:05.008 --> 00:01:09.210
won a war for their independence in 1783.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.850
Colonial elites like Thomas Jefferson,

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:14.390
who would later become a
United States president,

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:16.180
fueled the revolt by contributing

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:18.263
their resources toward reform.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:23.180
Frustration among the masses also plays

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.818
a critical role in social upheavals.

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:28.108
When a large percentage of a population

00:01:28.108 --> 00:01:30.440
feels grave discontent
with their political,

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:34.899
economic, and social
institutions, they may revolt.

00:01:34.899 --> 00:01:38.189
Only a few years after
the American Revolution,

00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:42.515
the people of France
initiated their own revolt.

00:01:42.515 --> 00:01:46.230
Several factors, including
economic difficulties

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.759
and an antiquated feudal system

00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:49.688
that fueled social inequalities

00:01:49.688 --> 00:01:52.930
all contributed to the dissent.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:56.840
Ultimately, French society
permanently ousted their monarchy

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.653
and replaced it with a republic.

00:02:01.489 --> 00:02:04.305
Another characteristic
found in revolutions

00:02:04.305 --> 00:02:06.300
is a shared motivation.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.239
Shared motivations are what unify

00:02:08.239 --> 00:02:10.128
a large enough number of people,

00:02:10.128 --> 00:02:12.600
specifically from multiple classes

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.793
and groups, to effectively rebel.

00:02:15.694 --> 00:02:17.829
These motivations helped the revolutions

00:02:17.829 --> 00:02:21.139
of Latin America in
the early 19th century.

00:02:21.139 --> 00:02:23.789
Ruled by Spain and Portugal at the time,

00:02:23.789 --> 00:02:27.070
colonists from multiple
Latin American classes

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:30.363
and ethnicities were inspired
by the Enlightenment.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:33.669
The intellectual movement
challenged tradition,

00:02:33.669 --> 00:02:36.019
including traditional forms of governance,

00:02:36.019 --> 00:02:38.440
and ended up playing a role in the fight

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:41.263
for colonists' independence
in Latin America.

00:02:43.947 --> 00:02:47.908
Severe state crises also
motivate revolutions.

00:02:47.908 --> 00:02:50.480
In particular, an administration's failure

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.928
to meet the needs of its people

00:02:51.928 --> 00:02:55.114
make it vulnerable to insurgency.

00:02:55.114 --> 00:02:58.739
The revolutions of early
20th century Russia occurred

00:02:58.739 --> 00:03:02.442
because of the government's
exceptional frailty.

00:03:02.442 --> 00:03:05.258
Its political, military,
and economic systems

00:03:05.258 --> 00:03:07.323
had been virtually decimated

00:03:07.323 --> 00:03:09.930
by the state's defeats in World War I.

00:03:11.245 --> 00:03:14.758
The nation's power vacuum
then led to revolts

00:03:14.758 --> 00:03:17.245
that replaced Russia's imperial state

00:03:17.245 --> 00:03:22.245
and created the world's
first communist regime.

00:03:24.498 --> 00:03:29.498
Virtually all revolutions
experience severe state crises,

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:31.693
shared motivations,

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.922
mass frustrations,

00:03:34.922 --> 00:03:38.818
and a dissident elite to some degree.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:42.730
While revolutions may
involve different players,

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:47.730
governments, and cultures,
the characteristics they share

00:03:47.808 --> 00:03:50.110
help them transcend their differences

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:53.983
and demonstrate the dynamism
of human nature and politics.

